{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N1U9L1bn57YmcJhNTsNMbK","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>[Truncated: PARTIAL view â€” showing lines 1-366 of 510 total (29564 tokens, cap 25000). Call Read with offset=367 limit=366 for the next page, or Grep to find a specific section. Do NOT answer from this page alone if the answer may be further in the file.]</system-reminder>\n\n1\t# Master Rollout Plan v5 â€” Agent-First and the v0â€“v1â€“v2 Ladder\n2\t\n3\t**Date:** 2026-05-14\n4\t**Status:** **MASTER** (living document). Synthesized from two parallel Cowork sessions that independently produced v5 drafts on 2026-05-14; the more-developed post-Pass-2 draft forms ~95% of this substrate, with surgical improvements pulled from the leaner proto. Further refinement happens *during execution* and is surfaced via `LIVING-GAPS.md` (created when the first execution-time gap surfaces) or direct edits to this file.\n5\t**Bounded-iteration discipline holds: no Pass 3.** Two critique passes (2026-05-14 morning) are the load-bearing review. Execution teaches the rest.\n6\t**Supersedes:** [Master Rollout Plan v4 â€” Pilots, Plasticity, and the Path to Production (May 5 2026)](./Master%20Rollout%20Plan%20v4%20â€”%20Pilots,%20Plasticity,%20and%20the%20Path%20to%20Production%20%28May%205%202026%29.md) (v4.2 addendum 2026-05-08).\n7\t**Companion:** [GAPS-2026-05-14.md](./GAPS-2026-05-14.md) â€” what v5 keeps / drops / defers / supersedes from v4. Frozen at master-promotion; emerging gaps go to `LIVING-GAPS.md`.\n8\t**Critique provenance:** [CRITIQUE-PASS-1-v5-proto.md](./CRITIQUE-PASS-1-v5-proto.md), [CRITIQUE-PASS-2-v5-proto.md](./CRITIQUE-PASS-2-v5-proto.md).\n9\t**Archived source drafts:** [archive/v5-drafts/MASTER-PLAN-v5--parallel-session-post-Pass2.md](./archive/v5-drafts/MASTER-PLAN-v5--parallel-session-post-Pass2.md) (the post-Pass-2 draft, ~95% of this content) and [archive/v5-drafts/PLAN-Master-Rollout-v5-proto-2026-05-14--session-A.md](./archive/v5-drafts/PLAN-Master-Rollout-v5-proto-2026-05-14--session-A.md) (the leaner proto, retained for the few framing improvements pulled forward).\n10\t**Inputs consumed:**\n11\t- [SESSION-HANDOFF-V5-Plan-Draft-2026-05-13.md](./SESSION-HANDOFF-V5-Plan-Draft-2026-05-13.md) â€” 18 locked decisions, parked list, definition of done\n12\t- [V5-RETRO-Brainstorm-2026-05-13.md](./V5-RETRO-Brainstorm-2026-05-13.md) â€” 26 entries of John+Claude dialogue that derived the locked decisions\n13\t- [STATE-OF-PROJECT-2026-05-13.md](./STATE-OF-PROJECT-2026-05-13.md) â€” v4-state ledger\n14\t- [PLAN-expert-coder-Win11-2026-05-13.md](./PLAN-expert-coder-Win11-2026-05-13.md) â†’ realized as the `expert-coder-Win11` skill, 2026-05-14\n15\t- [CLAUDE.md](./CLAUDE.md) â€” workspace orientation\n16\t- Workspace memory (`feedback_powershell_51_compat`, `gwl_server_hardware`, `skills_live_in_dev`, `feedback_terse_status`)\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## Versioning convention (canonical â€” see [VERSIONING.md](./VERSIONING.md))\n21\t\n22\tThe GWL **system version** is `v<B>.<H>`: **B** = t2r **brain** generation, **H** = agentic **harness/capacity** generation (OpenClaw + G-Brain + Helping Hand/Aurora). **Current: `v2.1`** = gen-2 dynamic-context t2r brain (implemented + live, verified 2026-05-24/25) + gen-1 harness.\n23\t\n24\t- Build iterations *within* a generation are tracked by date+commit, **not** by a version digit. Earlier \"v2.2 / v2.3 / v2.5\" labels were gen-2 **brain build** iterations mislabeled as system bumps â€” corrected to: the system is `v2.1`, the brain is gen-2.\n25\t- This is **orthogonal** to the **v0â€“v1â€“v2 agent-rollout ladder** in this plan's title (the ladder = agent/deliverable maturity stage). The agent `alpha-v0` is a **v0-ladder vehicle** that runs the **`v2.1` system**. Agent id â‰  system version.\n26\t\n27\t## Headline\n28\t\n29\t**v4 was brain-first. v5 is agent-first.** The brain layer is GWL's moat and is in good enough shape to start v0 today; the agent layer is commoditized and we're going to borrow Tan's GBrain wholesale. **v0's explicit goal is to replace Cowork for daily work** â€” Alpha as the v0 vehicle, t2r dispatcher (taste â†’ reasoning, both halves top-tier frontier), GBrain underneath, quality-signal hooks at every seam. Days-to-weeks to v0, not months.\n30\t\n31\t---\n32\t\n33\t## Update â€” 2026-05-27: t2r cost diagnosis â†’ Sovereign t2r Harness convergence\n34\t\n35\t**Status:** new direction locked; software plan next. Supersedes the v5 headline's \"borrow Tan's GBrain *wholesale* at the agent layer\" â€” see the reframe at the end of this block.\n36\t\n37\tA week-long cost problem on the daily-use agents (Ecgberht turns appearing to cost $0.45â€“$10.11) was root-caused and the path forward converged across three multi-round, multi-agent debates + OpenClaw SDK ground-truth spikes + cost simulations. Findings (all verified, not asserted):\n38\t\n39\t- **The cost meter was lying, not the brain.** The gateway client priced every turn at the configured fallback model (Sonnet) and ignored the cache split, overstating cost **3â€“10Ã—** (the \"$10.11\" turn really cost ~$1.07). MoE tiering AND prompt caching already work on the gateway (ledger: 85kâ€“1.98M cache_read tokens). **Fixed + live-verified** (truthful per-turn cost, real model/tier, cache-hit%); see `PLAN-Reporting-Accuracy-2026-05-27.md`.\n40\t- **The real cost/latency driver is the within-turn agentic tool-loop**, which OpenClaw cannot tier per step (it fixes one model per run) and whose framework overhead (~8.6s warm; auth + per-turn tool-registry rebuild) is large. SDK spikes: no stable `executeTool` (OpenClaw is an MCP *client*); `subagent.run` is the only stable way to reuse OpenClaw's stateful tools; `ownsCompaction:true` fires per-iteration compaction on the gateway path.\n41\t- **Convergence (mine + two external efforts):** build a **Sovereign t2r Harness** â€” a custom loop the agent fully owns, running a **recursive t2r cycle at every ReAct step** (the validated gold standard, `GOLD-STANDARD-T2R-Recursive-Agentic-Loop.md`). **Key correction:** do NOT swap *remote* reasoning models mid-loop (cross-model cache cold-start = measured **+120â€“242%**); win instead via free-local observation **compression** + **local sub-decisions ($0)** + **one cache-stable remote model per loop**.\n42\t- **Final spec:** `REPORT-Sovereign-t2r-Harness-Gold-Standard-FINAL.md` â€” per-agent **Soul** (cache-stable file), **persistent 3-tier memory** (episodic/semantic/procedural, written by free local models, retrieved into the message tail), **tiered tools** (basic in-harness via off-the-shelf MCP; complex/stateful delegated to OpenClaw via `subagent.run`, migrated in over time).\n43\t- **G-Brain reframe (the strategy change vs the v5 headline):** GBrain is installed but is **demoted from \"the agent layer\" to a deferred, offline training flywheel** that distills the harness's own cheap local tier from the `g27-v3` envelopes the harness emits â€” **never in the per-turn hot loop** (Bun-leak rule). v5 planned to borrow GBrain wholesale *as* the agent layer; the convergence builds our own sovereign agent layer instead and keeps GBrain for what it's uniquely good at (offline LoRA/distillation).\n44\t\n45\t**Decision:** go directly to Phase 2 (build the Sovereign t2r Harness). Next artifact: the module-by-module software plan. Session log: `SESSION-LOG-2026-05-27-t2r-harness-convergence.md`.\n46\t\n47\t---\n48\t\n49\t## 1. The v4 â†’ v5 reframe (load-bearing)\n50\t\n51\t**Status:** locked\n52\t\n53\tv4 mostly designed a *brain*. The tasteâ†’reasoning architecture, the cognitive cells, the plasticity catalog (26 mutations across 5 layers â€” not v4's prose-claimed 17), the curriculum-driven training, the adjudicator and its training tuples, the distillation losses, the drift detection â€” all of it is *cognition substrate*. v4 calls this work \"the path to production\" but production of *what* was hand-waved: the same plan also gestures at clusters of W/S/Math agents using the brain, but never separated the agent layer from the brain layer.\n54\t\n55\t**The single deepest cut in this review (Retro Entry 1 â†’ Entry 14):** brain â‰  agent. The agent is the persistent operating unit that *uses* a brain to do work â€” it has its own memory, skills, tools, planning loop, quality-signal pipeline, and ongoing identity. v4 fused the two; v5 pries them apart.\n56\t\n57\tThree corollaries flow from the reframe:\n58\t\n59\t1. **The agent layer is commoditized; the GWL brain is the moat.** Anthropic, Google, OpenAI, and a dozen frameworks (LangGraph, Letta, CrewAI, AutoGen, Cowork, Claude Code) have collectively spent hundreds of engineer-years on the agent layer. GWL needs *best-in-class* at this layer but does not need to be *innovative* here. The tasteâ†’reasoning brain, the cognitive cell substrate, the in-harness brain-training pipeline â€” those are differentiated and worth defending. Everything else: borrow.\n60\t2. **GBrain (Garry Tan's, MIT, 11.1kâ˜…, OpenClaw-native, released 2026-04-05) delivers ~80% of v0's agent-layer scope** in a 30-minute install. 29 baseline skills + Git-versioned markdown Brain Repo + pgvector retrieval + dream cycle + entity-tier escalation + `skillify` workflow + `Minions` job queue + MCP server. GBrain is purpose-built for the runtime John has chosen and is open-source under terms compatible with this workspace. **Adopting GBrain replaces months of v4-implied build-effort at the agent layer.**\n61\t3. **GBrain does NOT deliver the quality-signal capture loop.** No skill success-rate scoring, no Wilson-CI tournaments at the agent layer, no RLHF/DPO, no 5-flavor signals (outcome / user / resource / self-consistency / replay). This is *the* v5 GWL addition: hook-layer instrumentation at GBrain's skill and dream-cycle boundaries that captures the five signals and feeds them into both the GWL brain-training pipeline AND GBrain's skill-improvement workflow.\n62\t\n63\tThe clean way to say what v5 *is*: **assemble best-in-class agent-layer commodity beneath a GWL t2r brain, instrument the seam with quality-signal hooks, and use the result for daily work while the brain continues to deepen underneath.**\n64\t\n65\t---\n66\t\n67\t## 2. Current state recap\n68\t\n69\t**Status:** locked (consumed from STATE-OF-PROJECT-2026-05-13; tooling additions through 2026-05-14)\n70\t\n71\t### Brain layer (v4's territory) â€” substantially advanced\n72\t\n73\tWave 7 closed across three phases on 2026-05-08/09. Test gate moved 315 â†’ 374 â†’ 442 â†’ **498/498/0/0**. All scoped Wave-7 gaps closed: G-24 integrator-fuse, G-25 best-in-class skills, G-26 distillation losses, G-27 training-capture envelope, G-28 skill-evolution disabled-shell (gated off in Phase B), G-29 replay scheduler, G-31 drift-judge expert, G-32 adjudicator-tuple corpus. The Adjudicator-training-tuple corpus has been accumulating since 2026-05-08 â€” 5+ days of real capture data.\n74\t\n75\tPlasticity catalog landed 2026-05-07 (Session 6: 26 mutation IDs across 5 layers, despite v4 prose saying 17). Plasticity proposer skeleton landed 2026-05-07 (Session 7).\n76\t\n77\tPhase A foundations shipped 2026-05-07 (alpha-linear and alpha-lorentz pilot duo, SOULs at STRICT parity, per-agent page route, Phase B plan committed with `eng-1-9` u01-u03 unit slice locked). Linux smoke green; Windows smoke not yet confirmed.\n78\t\n79\tCURR-1 audit tool shipped 2026-05-07 (`audit-completeness.py`, 18 tests). The cp1252 / curly-quotes bug that ate the first audit pass is now fixed.\n80\t\n81\tPhase B first GLCI cadence ran 2026-05-07 evening (baseline 4/6 on both pilots, threshold 0.85).\n82\t\n83\t### Hardware â€” better than v4 anticipated\n84\t\n85\tHost migrated laptop â†’ **gwl-server** on 2026-05-12. Dell XPS 8960, i9-13900K (24c/32t), 32 GB DDR5 (single-DIMM punch-list item: matched second stick ~$80-100), RTX 4070 12 GB Ada, 1.8 TB OS NVMe + 1.9 TB workspace NVMe. Tailscale-served at `https://gwl.tailb49f65.ts.net`. **v4's INFRA-1 cloud-VM plan is moot** â€” the 12 GB VRAM on the 4070 caps Phase C at QLoRA on â‰¤8B students, which is exactly the design target for the local-distillation workstream.\n86\t\n87\tPhase C Step A scripts authored 2026-05-13 (paused per John's request, not blocking v5): `Install-Phase-C-Stack.ps1` + `smoke_qlora.py`. Decisions locked: Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct + Miniconda + Python 3.12 + cu130 wheels + D:\\ for venv & weights.\n88\t\n89\t### Agent layer (v5's territory) â€” paper, but two enablers landed today\n90\t\n91\t`alpha` exists as an OpenClaw agent (Gemini-backed, 5 skills, sub-30s `hi` response after the 2026-04-30 recovery). `prime-coder` and `sigma` are operational. **Everything else in the agent registry is paper** â€” W/S/Math clusters are persona files, no spawned worker agent has run. The \"cluster operation\" v4 promised has not begun.\n92\t\n93\t`project-manager-kit` shipped 2026-05-07 and evolved substantially on 2026-05-13 during the anchor-coach pilot. Real-Intent Protocol (Parable of the Oranges) + Run-don't-narrate + use-claude-code skill + nine other T1/T2/T3 edits landed. Canonical relocated to `C:\\dev\\Project-Manager\\`; the Agentic-Home copy needs a one-way-sync resolution in S1.\n94\t\n95\t**Two enablers landed today (2026-05-14) that change v5 viability:**\n96\t\n97\t- **`expert-coder-Win11` skill shipped** â€” SKILL.md + 8 references + `Test-Win11Environment.ps1` (now bridge-aware after a real-host verification bug-fix this session) + CRITIQUE-PASS-1.md. All five mirror locations match by MD5 (canonical `C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11\\`, `skills-master\\`, `.claude\\skills\\`, `.gemini\\skills\\`, `~\\.openclaw\\skills\\`). Alpha and Prime Coder personas updated. Memory entry `skill_windows_coding` committed. Bootstrap auto-discovery confirmed (line 134 of Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1 picks up any `skills-master\\<name>\\SKILL.md` without explicit reference).\n98\t- **Coworkâ†”host PowerShell bridge is LIVE** (`mcp__Claude_Code_Bridge__run_command`). Destructive-op gating + admin-elevation flagging built in. Eliminates the paste-prompt failure mode the V5-RETRO flagged as the existential risk to execution time. Every v5 sprint task can now write *and run* host scripts directly.\n99\t\n100\tTogether these two reduce v5's \"what could go wrong at the Windows host\" risk class materially. Most Â§4 S1 tasks below assume the bridge is available; if it were not, S1 would need ~30% more elapsed time.\n101\t\n102\t### What this means for v5 sequencing\n103\t\n104\tThe brain layer has more than enough runway to start v0 right now without further brain work. The brain work *should continue in parallel* (the in-harness corpus that v0 produces is the input to the next brain-training cycle), but it does not gate v0. **The bottleneck is agent-layer work, not brain-layer work.**\n105\t\n106\t---\n107\t\n108\t## 3. The v0 / v1 / v2 spec table\n109\t\n110\t**Status:** locked (consumed from Retro Entry 15-18; walkthrough-confirmed with John 2026-05-14)\n111\t\n112\tThe critical path is one agent's ladder, not a phase-cluster arc. Specialization (cluster operation, W/S/Math agents) happens *after* v0 is in daily use.\n113\t\n114\t| Version | Agent layer | Brain layer | Sleep updates | Wallet (revised) | Gate to promote |\n115\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n116\t| **v0** | OpenClaw runtime + GBrain (Tan's, v0.19+) on top with native `AGENTS.md` resolver at workspace root, t2r dispatcher as a brain-layer module GBrain calls. Best-in-class skill bundle (see Â§4). **Cowork-comparable for John's daily use.** Vehicle is the **`alpha-v0`** agent (shipped 2026-05-16 commits `6250cf5a` + `6482d06d`; separate tile and routing entry from the legacy `alpha` agent which still routes to the brain-research v2 orchestrator). In addition to alpha-v0 (the general-purpose vehicle), the v0 architecture supports **v0 specialists** â€” sibling agents with a different skill bundle + persona prompt + optional default project binding. Same dispatcher, same model defaults, same wallet. See Â§13 for the workstream cadence and Â§4 S2/S3 for the rollout. | t2r architecture: two sequential frontier calls per turn. Taste first (curate + sharp-query + skill/resource hint), then reasoning (execute against the curated context). No cognitive cells yet, no local LLMs. **Both halves top-tier frontier** â€” default **Gemini Pro both**, with **Anthropic Opus** available per-agent / per-turn for high-value escalation. Smart cheap/expensive routing is a v1+ capability, not v0. | Agent skills (success-rate scoring, retire low-performers â€” **human-in-loop through v0, no auto-retire**; aligns with GBrain's stated \"human-stays-in-the-loop\" philosophy), tools (usage stats, capability ranking), hooks (threshold tuning from outcomes). **No brain-side training in v0** â€” both halves are frontier-driven. | **$100/month per active agent** (soft alert at $80, hard cap enforced at the dispatcher with graceful-degrade + interactive cap-override). **Scope: measures t2r dispatcher calls only.** GBrain's internal LLM + embedding usage is a *separate* line item (see \"GBrain operational wallet\" note below the table). Cowork reference: $200/mo flat. **Revision triggers:** first soft-alert hit, OR end of S1 review, OR John reports cap is friction. Revision = `routing.json` commit + log entry in `logs/wallet-revisions.jsonl`. **Precedence:** raise the wallet, do not downgrade models. | **Per-workflow-type adoption matrix** (code / research / drafting / finance / trip-planning / project-management each tracked separately) replaces binary \"is John using it.\" Promotion to v1 = â‰¥3 workflow types showing â‰¥50% v0 adoption with stable signal quality. |\n117\t| **v1** | Same as v0. | t2r with **cognitive cells** for taste-cell and reasoning-cell. Each cell still frontier-driven (no local LLMs). Cell substrate provides MoE-style expert routing inside each half. | Everything v0 sleeps **+** cognitive-cell config (gate residuals, expert routing inside cells, atlas concept reorganization). Still no LoRA â€” brain weights are not changing. | Same as v0 in expectation; cell substrate adds ~10% routing overhead amortized. | Cell substrate stably outperforms v0 on the same trust-ladder tasks for **2 weeks**. Cell-config sleep mutations demonstrably improving metric. |\n118\t| **v2** | Same as v0. | v1 cognitive cells **+** local QLoRA-trained 8B student per cell (taste-student, reasoning-student) on the gwl-server 4070. **Gating function** decides per turn: local student vs frontier escalation. First neural plasticity. | Everything v1 sleeps **+** LoRA on the local students from the in-harness training corpus **+** gating-function calibration (when to escalate). | Wallet shrinks: gating diverts ~40-60% of turns to local students (~$0.001/turn) vs frontier (~$0.01-0.05/turn). Per-agent monthly burn target: **$300-700**. | Local students serve â‰¥40% of turns at â‰¥90% quality parity (measured via held-out frontier-judge). Gating function calibrated (escalates correctly on hard turns). |\n119\t\n120\tAfter v2 works on a single agent, GWL is in position to evaluate the full-brain rollout. After v0 works, **specialization can begin in parallel** with v1/v2 brain deepening â€” W/S/Math clusters as additional v0-shaped agents with specialty skill bundles.\n121\t\n122\t**GBrain operational wallet (separate from t2r wallet):** GBrain's own LLM and embedding-API usage during normal operation â€” dream cycle entity escalation, classifier fail-improve loop, retrieval embeddings â€” is tracked as a second wallet, distinct from v0's $100/mo t2r budget. Initial size: **$30/month** per active GBrain install. Audit task lands in S2 to right-size against real-use data. Confusion-avoidance rationale: a wallet-cap-hit in this line item should not be misread as v0 t2r failure; they are independently sized and tracked.\n123\t\n124\t### Resolution of seven drafting-time questions (walkthrough-locked 2026-05-14)\n125\t\n126\t1. **v0 wallet sizing.** **$100/month per active agent.** Soft alert at $80, hard cap enforced at the dispatcher with graceful-degrade behavior. Reference point: Cowork delivers comparable daily output at $200/mo flat, so v0 must demonstrate value at half that. Re-derive from observed envelope after one week of S1 data. **Precedence rule:** if $100 proves too tight for top-tier-both (Q2), *raise the wallet* â€” do not downgrade models. Per-skill cost attribution lands in S2.\n127\t2. **Same vs different models for taste vs reasoning.** **Top-tier frontier on both halves.** Default: Gemini Pro both (cost math fits the $100 cap at ~30-300 turns/day). Anthropic Opus available per-agent and per-turn for high-value escalation. Smart cheap/expensive routing is genuinely a v1+ capability â€” v2's local-student-vs-frontier gating is exactly this kind of routing, and conflating it with v0 dilutes the t2r-architecture-purity demonstration that v0 exists to prove.\n128\t3. **Naming collision.** Local `gbrain/` (and `gbrain-lite/`) renames to `gwl-runtime/` (and `gwl-runtime-lite/`). Tan's GBrain takes its native `gbrain/`. **Three-path disambiguation per Pass 2 B-11:** workspace-root, `$env:USERPROFILE\\gbrain\\` (the user-profile training-data root referenced in 30+ brain-code files), and Tan's GBrain install location are *three separate locations*. Spec memo `PATH-RENAME-design.md` precedes execution; lands S1 days 2-3.\n129\t4. **Migration order.** **GBrain first.** Install OpenClaw + GBrain on gwl-server (S1 days 4-5), validate dream-cycle, then build t2r as a brain-layer module that GBrain's skill router invokes (S1 days 6-7). The t2r dispatcher is shaped to fit GBrain's `pre_turn` / `post_turn` hooks, not the reverse. **Schema extension to `routing.json` for per-half model fields (taste-model, reasoning-model) is load-bearing for the t2r dispatcher and must land in S1 day-8 regardless of cross-provider exercise.** Cross-provider wallet plumbing (Opus-escalation path) defers to S2.\n130\t5. **First task / trust-ladder.** **No staged trust-ladder.** v0 ships as a general-purpose daily-use agent and John uses it for whatever comes up. **Success criterion is a per-workflow-type adoption matrix** â€” code, research, drafting, finance, trip-planning, project-management each tracked independently â€” not a binary \"is John using it.\" If 3+ types show â‰¥50% v0 adoption with stable signal quality, promotion to v1 is open. The 5-flavor signal capture (JSONL) runs task-agnostic so the matrix derives from real data, not survey questions. If v0 broadly fails across most types, the answer is *rethink the architecture* â€” see Â§11 Failure-mode contingencies.\n131\t6. **v0 vehicle.** **The existing `alpha` agent becomes the v0 vehicle.** Alpha is already running, already in `routing.json`, already loads the v0 starter skill set, already has wallet plumbing. The persona-vs-reality gap (Retro Entry 6's \"Gap A â€” Capability\") is solvable by editing Alpha's persona to honestly describe what v0-Alpha does â€” **but the rewrite is its own design exercise**, captured in a separate design memo `PERSONA-DESIGN-Alpha-v0.md` authored in S1 day-1/2 before the conversion task. **Alpha's `routing.json` entry must explicitly upgrade to top-tier model per half per Q2** â€” current entry is Gemini Flash (post-2026-04-30 recovery); v0 requires Gemini Pro both halves as default, Opus available per-turn. `alpha-linear` and `alpha-lorentz` (the brain-research pilot duo) stay on their separate track â€” they're SOUL-twin pilots for Phase B brain work, not the daily-use vehicle.\n132\t7. **Cadence.** **Sprints and Brain Waves run in parallel.** Sprint S1, S2, â€¦ (~2-week units) for agent-layer v0/v1/v2 work, anchored to deliverables. Brain Wave 8+ for brain-side work (corpus-fed distillation, plasticity activation, drift refinement), anchored to test-gate jumps. Different work shapes deserve different cadences; forcing both into one taxonomy mislabels what's being tracked.\n133\t\n134\t---\n135\t\n136\t## 4. The v0 build plan â€” concrete, dated, decomposed\n137\t\n138\t**Status:** master (incorporating Pass 1 + Pass 2 amendments)\n139\t\n140\t### Sprint S1 â€” Foundation (target 2026-05-15 through 2026-06-04, 3 weeks)\n141\t\n142\t3 weeks: weeks 1-2 deliverables (5/15-5/29), week 3 catch-up + S2 prep (5/30-6/4). Slack is a feature â€” week 3 absorbs the unknowns concentrated in the rename + GBrain install days. If everything green by end of week 2, week 3 starts S2 early; that's a win, not lost time.\n143\t\n144\t| Day | Task | Verify gate |\n145\t|---|---|---|\n146\t| 5/15 | (a) Author `PERSONA-DESIGN-Alpha-v0.md` design memo â€” drops cluster-dispatch promises, defines what v0-Alpha actually does as a t2r general-purpose daily-use agent, decides what survives from current persona vs what's redesigned. (b) Run Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1 on host to propagate `expert-coder-Win11`. (c) Mirror `skills-master\\expert-coder-Win11\\` â†’ canonical `C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11\\`. *Note: (b) and (c) already complete as of session that promoted this plan; verify state matches and check off.* | Design memo committed. `openclaw skills info expert-coder-Win11` returns the skill from a *fresh* PS session. `Test-Path C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11\\SKILL.md` is True. |\n147\t| 5/16 | Sync `C:\\dev\\Project-Manager\\` (canonical) â†’ `Agentic-Home\\skills-master\\project-manager\\` (direction is canonical â†’ propagation, not bidirectional). Re-run Bootstrap to propagate to runtime mirrors. | `diff -r` between source and propagated copy returns empty. `openclaw skills info project-manager` returns the skill. |\n148\t| 5/16-5/17 | **B-11: Namespace rename (multi-location).** Author `PATH-RENAME-design.md` spec (half-day). Then execute the three-location disambiguation: (a) `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\gbrain\\` â†’ `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\gwl-runtime\\` (workspace-root runtime state); (b) `Move-Item C:\\Users\\john\\gbrain C:\\Users\\john\\gwl-corpus -Verbose` (brain training-data root; preserves 5+ days of Wave-7 corpus); (c) leave a hole for Tan's GBrain to claim workspace-root `gbrain/` post-install. Scripted find-and-replace `'gbrain'` â†’ `'gwl-corpus'` across the brain tree (30+ files); update CLAUDE.md \"Don't-touch list\" + `.gitignore` + memory entries. **Test gate stays green post-rename.** | (a) Brain test suite still 498/498/0/0 post-rename. (b) `grep -r \"['\\\"]gbrain['\\\"]\" sandbox-lab-gui\\brain` returns zero hits. (c) Wave-7 corpus accessible at new path: `Test-Path C:\\Users\\john\\gwl-corpus\\agents\\alpha-linear\\adjudicator-training-tuples\\*` is True. |\n149\t| 5/18 | **Bun runtime install + bootstrap integration.** `winget install Oven-sh.Bun --silent --disable-interactivity --accept-package-agreements --accept-source-agreements`. Verify `bun --version`. Pin version in `Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1` (new section). Document in CLAUDE.md: \"use `bun` *only* for GBrain operations; `npm`/`node` for everything else.\" | `bun --version` returns expected version. `Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1` re-run picks up Bun install state. CLAUDE.md mentions Bun scope. |\n150\t| 5/19-5/20 | Install OpenClaw + GBrain on gwl-server. `git clone https://github.com/garrytan/gbrain` (default branch `master`) + `bun install && bun link` â€” **NOT `bun install -g`** (README explicitly forbids; postinstall hook breakage). Set `HF_TOKEN` + OpenAI/Anthropic keys in GBrain's `.env`. Set `OPENCLAW_WORKSPACE=C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home` env (per Q-F finding). Run `gbrain doctor`. | `gbrain doctor` reports green. `gbrain serve` (MCP stdio) responds to a tool list. Dream cycle has run at least once. Tan's GBrain owns workspace-root `gbrain/`. |\n151\t| 5/21 | **Write `AGENTS.md` at workspace root** per Q-F finding (GBrain v0.19+ native support). ~10 lines: points skill resolution at `skills-master/`, per-agent personas at `Sandbox Setup Package/PERSONAS/global/<id>-personal-manager.md`. This *is* the GBrainâ†”GWL bridge. | `gbrain check-resolvable --verbose` returns zero unreachable errors. GWL skills auto-detected from `skills-master/` walk. |\n152\t| 5/22-5/23 | **Schema extension + t2r dispatcher.** Extend `routing.json` for per-half model fields (`taste_model`, `reasoning_model`); update Settings Vault GET/POST. Author t2r dispatcher as a GBrain-compatible module â€” receives raw input â†’ calls taste model with skill-hint context â†’ receives sharp-query + curated context + optional skill/resource hint â†’ calls reasoning model â†’ returns answer. Atomic logging writes G-27 envelope shape (per Q-H finding) with `source: 'v0-t2r'` annotation (B-15) and `mode: 'practice'`. | Smoke test: `node t2r-dispatcher.mjs --input \"what is 7*8?\"` returns 56 with envelope row in `C:\\Users\\john\\gwl-corpus\\agents\\alpha\\adjudicator-training-tuples\\<date>\\<id>.ndjson`. Schema extension shows up in Settings Vault UI. |\n153\t| 5/24 | Install the v0 starter skill bundle into GBrain via `gbrain skillpack install`. Starter: `deep-think`, `deep-research`, `expert-coder`, `expert-coder-Win11`, `project-manager`, `use-claude-code`, `family-accountant`. Anthropic marketplace: `docx`, `pdf`, `pptx`, `xlsx`, `frontend-design`. Third-party (Skills.sh): `valyu`, `schedule`. | `gbrain skills list` returns all of the above. `gbrain check-resolvable` returns zero unreachable errors. |\n154\t| 5/26 | **Alpha conversion (executes design memo from 5/15).** Rewrite `Sandbox Setup Package\\PERSONAS\\global\\alpha-personal-manager.md` per design memo. Update Alpha's `routing.json` entry: `taste_model: gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, `reasoning_model: gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, with Opus available as per-turn override. Wire Alpha to GBrain's resolver (now native via AGENTS.md). | `openclaw agent --agent alpha --local -m \"hi\"` returns a t2r-routed response with both halves logged at top-tier model strings. Persona file matches reality. |\n155\t| 5/27 | **Signal-capture