c: `PLAN-Master-Plan-Update-Specialists-2026-05-16.md` Â§B. |\n| Sleep loop (agent-layer) | Implement first sleep mutation: skill success-rate scoring with Wilson intervals; **demote skills below threshold by surfacing for John's approval â€” no auto-retire** (per Pass 1 Q-A; aligned with GBrain \"human-stays-in-the-loop\" philosophy). |\n| **GBrain operational wallet audit** | Per B-12 â€” audit GBrain's actual API spend (LLM dream-cycle calls, embedding API, classifier fail-improve loops) on real-use data. Right-size the GBrain wallet from the $30/mo starting estimate. |\n| Wallet enforcement (extension) | Per-agent monthly burn dashboard. Per-skill cost attribution surfaces top-cost skills. Now scoped per (agent Ã— month) which includes alpha-v0 + each specialist independently. |\n| Specialist tile-collapse decision | At S2 close, decide: keep v0 specialists as their own AgentMatrix sub-row (current default), or collapse them into the alpha-v0 tile with project-bound auto-specialist-pick? Default recommendation: keep them as sibling tiles in S2; reconsider at S3 close. |\n| Cleanup | Resolve project-manager-kit canonical divergence (if not done in S1). Audit alpha-v0 + first specialists' personas against actual usage patterns from S2 signal data (validation, not redesign). |\n| Cadence-sync | Weekly entries in `logs/cadence-sync/` â€” the new fourth bullet (Specialist track state per Â§12) starts being meaningful in week 2 once finance-alpha + code-alpha are running. |\n\n**S2 success criterion:** Per-workflow-type adoption matrix produced from real signal data. Numerical answer per type, not a vibe. Green = 3+ workflow types showing â‰¥50% v0 adoption with stable signal quality. If S2 review finds v0 fell short on most types, S3 reshapes per Â§11 contingencies.\n\n### Sprint S3 â€” Polish + brain-track resumption (target 2026-06-19 through 2026-07-02, 2 weeks)\n\n| Theme | Tasks |\n|---|---|\n| **Bridge expansion** | Claude Code Bridge is LIVE since 2026-05-14. S3 expands bridge use cases: install/upgrade automation via the bridge; log collection; host-state probes; expert-coder-Win11 pre-flight runs against real host data. |\n| **v0 polish + missing-skill identification** | Read S2 signal data, identify the skills v0 lacks for John's actual workflows, install missing skills from marketplaces or author new ones via `skillify`. Mature the skill-demotion UX (still human-in-loop; auto-retire stays v1+). Both \"second v0-shaped agent\" and \"auto-retire\" dropped per Pass 1 Q-A + Q-B AMENDs. |\n| **v0 specialists (next 2-4)** | Read S2 per-workflow-type adoption matrix and pick 2-4 specialists from the workflow types showing clear v0 fumble (taste-call retrieval pulling wrong notes, reasoning-pass missing project-specific context, etc.). Candidate pool: `math-research-alpha`, `teaching-alpha`, `drafting-alpha`, `trip-planning-alpha`. **Do not pre-commit which 2-4** â€” decide at start of S3 from S2 data; ship in S3 weeks 1-2. Per-specialist construction template established in S2 (`PLAN-Specialists-v0-Pattern.md`); marginal cost ~1 day each. |\n| **Specialist demotion** | If a S2 specialist (`finance-alpha` or `code-alpha`) shows lower per-turn quality or lower John-use rate than generalist alpha-v0 on its own workflow type, flag for retirement and surface for John's approval. Auto-retire stays human-in-loop through v0 per master plan Â§7 Q-A. |\n| Brain layer (Brain Wave 8) | Resume Phase C Step A. Llama-3.1-8B QLoRA on gwl-server 4070, training on the now-rich adjudicator-tuple corpus (including v0 t2r contributions from S1-S2). This is *brain-layer work* running parallel with Sprint S3 agent-layer work. |\n| **Promote-to-v1 gate evaluation** | At S3 close: evaluate per-workflow-type adoption matrix accumulated across S2 + S3. If green per Â§3 promote criterion, scope S4 = v1 cognitive cells. If not green, scope S4 per Â§11 failure-mode branch. |\n| Cadence-sync | Weekly entries; closing entry summarizes Sprint + Brain Wave dependencies for S4. |\n\n**S3 success criterion:** Per-workflow-type matrix shows green (3+ types â‰¥50% adoption) â€” promote to v1 scope. OR red â€” invoke Â§11 branch (a/b/c). OR mixed â€” S4 = polish + targeted patch. Brain side: Phase C Step A green smoke (Llama-3.1-8B QLoRA training loop runs on the 4070 against the corpus).\n\n### Promote-to-v1 gate\n\nAfter S3 closes, evaluate against the v0 â†’ v1 promotion gate (table Â§3): per-workflow-type adoption matrix with â‰¥3 workflow types at â‰¥50% v0 adoption + stable signal quality + architecture demonstrably stable across real tasks. If green: scope S4 as v1 cognitive-cell substrate. If mixed (1-2 types working, others not): S4 = targeted patch + delay v1 by one sprint. If red (broad failure): invoke Â§11 failure-mode contingency â€” rethink experiment branches (a)/(b)/(c).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Parallel workstreams (where v4 work continues)\n\n**Status:** locked from STATE-OF-PROJECT + retro\n\nv4's brain work does not stop because v5 reorients. It continues *in parallel* with v0 build, on a different cadence (Brain Waves alongside Agent Sprints).\n\n| Workstream | v4 origin | v5 disposition | Cadence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Adjudicator-training-tuple corpus capture | Wave 7 Phase 2 (G-32) | **Continues** â€” this is the input to v2 and beyond. Already accumulating since 2026-05-08. | Runs continuously; no sprint allocation. |\n| Tier-3 distillation losses (G-26) | Wave 7 Phase 2 | **Continues** â€” distillation is needed for v2 local students. | Wired; runs on tuple ingestion. |\n| Replay scheduler (G-29) | Wave 7 Phase 2 | **Continues** â€” feeds the in-harness brain-training pipeline. | Wired; runs on tuple ingestion. |\n| Drift detection (G-31 drift-judge expert, Tier-1 watcher) | Wave 7 Phase 2-3 | **Continues** â€” drift dissipates via replay-scheduler boost, no auto-school flip. | Wired; runs continuously. |\n| G-28 skill-evolution enable | Wave 7 Phase 3 (gated off) | **Stays gated off in v5 until S3 at earliest**, then flip if the agent-layer skill-scoring is stable. | Sprint S3+ candidate. |\n| CURR-2 (Gemini gap-fill loop) | v4 Â§6.1 | **Defers** to S4+ â€” agent-layer work is the higher priority. The 5/7 stubs and gaps stay logged. | Not in v0 critical path. |\n| CURR-3 (curation pass) | v4 Â§6.1 | **Defers** to S4+ for the same reason. | Not in v0 critical path. |\n| Phase B Windows smoke | v4 Phase B | **Continues opportunistically** â€” happens when v0 build needs a Windows-smoke confirmation anyway. | Sprint S1-2 ambient. |\n| Phase B first GLCI cadence (post-baseline) | v4 Phase B | **Continues opportunistically** â€” alpha-linear/alpha-lorentz keep their research role. | Sprint S2+. |\n| Plasticity Session 8+ (validity rules, shadow-evaluator, proposal store, dashboard) | v4 / Session-7 roadmap | **Continues** with v4's cadence; not gated on v5. | Brain-Wave 8 (separate track from Sprint cadence). |\n| Phase C Step A (Llama-3.1-8B install) | Authored 2026-05-13, paused | **Resumes in S3** â€” concurrent with v0 trust accumulation. | Sprint S3 brain-layer slot. |\n| Phase C Step B (Tier-3 LoRA wiring) | v4 Phase C | **Sprint S4+** â€” gated on Step A. | Sprint S4. |\n| Punch-list infrastructure (Caddy install, LSASS ASR re-flip, ASR-loop bug in Setup-GWL-Server.ps1, second 32 GB DIMM) | STATE-OF-PROJECT Â§C | **Opportunistic** â€” pulled in when it blocks a sprint task; otherwise on the punch list. | Background. |\n\nThe brain-layer corpus accumulation is *invisible to John day-to-day* but is the substrate that v1 and v2 train on. **v0 producing real interactions is what makes v1 and v2 possible** â€” every v0 turn captured in JSONL is a future training pair.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The hooks meta-architecture\n\n**Status:** master (the hook surface is locked; the per-hook implementation is sprint work)\n\nPer Retro Entry 16, six hooks are load-bearing for v0 â€” the points in the agent loop where GWL's quality-signal capture latches into GBrain's runtime. These are not GWL inventions; they are the standard agent-runtime hook surface that LangGraph, Letta, AutoGen, and Claude Code itself expose. GWL's contribution is *what gets written to JSONL at each*.\n\n| Hook | What v0 writes there | What sleep does with it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `session_start` | Load relevant episodic memory for project; check tool availability; load `.pm/state.json`. | Update session-frequency stats per project. |\n| `pre_turn` | Retrieval over skill library; surface \"you did this before\" candidates; inject quality-scored skills into context (taste call). **Replay signal: extends GBrain's `eval_candidates` capture path** (with `GBRAIN_CONTRIBUTOR_MODE=1`, native since GBrain v0.25.0) rather than reimplementing â€” v5 inherits the retrieval-capture work GBrain already did. | Adjust similarity threshold for reuse-proposal (Retro Entry 16: \"hook thresholds become learnable parameters\"). |\n| `pre_tool_call` | Cost check (resource signal); confirm tool selection; possibly route to cheaper model. | Update tool-success stats per (task-type, tool). |\n| `post_tool_call` | Log outcome (resource signal: time/tokens); update skill score if tool was associated with a named skill. | Demote skills with low success rates; surface for retire. |\n| `post_turn` | The 5-flavor JSONL row: input, taste-output, reasoning-output, skills_used, tools_used, latency, cost, optional outcome-verifier result. | Tier-1 maintenance digest; Tier-3 brain-training pair if criteria met. |\n| `on_user_feedback` | User signal: approve / edit / reject / redo / silence-as-implicit-approve. | Back-propagate to skill scores; raise envelope for next sleep cycle. |\n| `on_error` | Capture error; route to fallback; surface to user with context. | Pattern-match errors over time; propose a `fix-it` skill via skillify. |\n| `session_end` | Episodic â†’ semantic consolidation; append session summary; refresh investor brief if stale. | Tier-2 consolidation step. |\n| `sleep_start` / `sleep_step` / `sleep_end` | Tier-1/2/3 sleep cycle entries (these already exist on the brain side from Wave 7). | This is where the agent learning actually happens â€” hook-threshold adjustments, skill score updates, hook-routing changes. |\n\nThe **load-bearing insight from Retro Entry 16** is that *hooks themselves are learnable*. The `pre_turn` similarity threshold for \"this is similar enough to reuse\" is a number. Sleep adjusts it based on outcomes. The agent learns its routing without retraining any model. This is the cheapest learning mechanism in the entire stack and is gross-margin-positive on day one of v0.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Open questions â€” fully resolved across Pass 1 + Pass 2\n\n**Status:** locked\n\nAll drafting-time questions Q1-Q7 are walkthrough-locked with John (see Â§3). The critique passes added Q-A through Q-N and resolved each:\n\n- **Q-A.** *Auto-retire timing.* AMEND â€” human-in-loop demotion through all of v0; auto-retire is v1+ capability when brain-side cell substrate adds signal. Aligns with GBrain's own \"human-stays-in-the-loop\" philosophy (Pass 2 B-17).\n- **Q-B.** *Second v0-shaped agent in S3.* AMEND â€” strike from S3 themes. Specialization happens *after* v0 lands (Retro Entry 15); S3 is when we find out if v0 works. Replaced with \"v0 polish + missing-skill identification from signal data.\"\n- ~~Q-C, Q-D, Q-I~~ obsolesced by walkthrough (wallet sizing locked at $100/$80; staged trust-ladder dropped).\n- **Q-E.** *Bun-only runtime readiness.* AMEND â€” escalated to dedicated S1 day-4 task (winget install + version pin + Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1 update + CLAUDE.md scope note \"use Bun only for GBrain operations\").\n- **Q-F.** *GBrain resolver contract.* KEEP-amended â€” Pass 2 research confirmed GBrain v0.19+ natively supports `AGENTS.md` at workspace root. Bridge reduces to ~10 lines + 1 env var (`OPENCLAW_WORKSPACE=C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`). S1 day-7 task.\n- **Q-G.** *Cross-provider routing schema.* AMEND â€” schema extension to `routing.json` for per-half model fields is **load-bearing for t2r** and lands S1 day-8 regardless of cross-provider exercise. Opus-cross-wallet plumbing defers to S2.\n- **Q-H.** *Capture envelope format.* AMEND-significantly â€” Pass 2 read `adjudicator-tuple-writer.mjs`; envelope's `brain` field already takes `'taste'|'reasoning'`. v0 t2r writes G-27 envelope natively with `source: 'v0-t2r'` annotation + `mode: 'practice'`. Triggers Pass 2 B-11 namespace finding.\n- **Q-J.** *Letta revisit.* KEEP-amended â€” sharper trigger: revisit only on (a) Pass 2 explicitly identifying GBrain memory as load-bearing failure, OR (b) S1 GBrain install spike failing. Pass 2 did not identify failure; trigger is dormant.\n- **Q-K.** *Graceful-degrade on cap-hit.* AMEND â€” specced into S1 day-14 wallet enforcement: refuse new taste call + preserve in-flight reasoning + **interactive cap-override** (\"approve $X overage for this turn?\") + logged rationale.\n- **Q-L.** *Post-finalization artifacts.* KEEP â€” confirmed Pass 2. Subplan-per-sprint (`plans/subplans/S<n>.md`) + `LIVING-GAPS.md` (or section of this file). Author once the first execution-time gap surfaces.\n- **Q-M.** *Three-`gbrain`-paths disambiguation.* AMEND-major (Pass 2 B-11) â€” split rename: `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\gbrain\\` â†’ `gwl-runtime\\`; `C:\\Users\\john\\gbrain\\` â†’ `gwl-corpus\\` (30+ brain-code files); Tan's GBrain takes workspace-root `gbrain/` post-install. Spec memo `PATH-RENAME-design.md` then execute, S1 days 2-3. Test gate stays green post-rename.\n- **Q-N.** *v0 t2r envelope downstream-feed.* AMEND â€” v0 t2r writes G-27 envelope with `source: 'v0-t2r'` annotation; downstream Tier-3 distillation queue + corpus readers filter by source. No format change; just an annotation extension.\n\nAll critique items resolved. Bounded-iteration discipline holds (Pass 1 + Pass 2 only).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Risk register\n\n**Status:** master\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GBrain proves harder to install / less stable than the 30-minute claim suggests | Medium | High (delays S1) | Spike GBrain install on a sacrificial subdirectory in S1 day 4; bail if green-smoke takes >1 day. **Vendor a known-good snapshot** of GBrain at workspace level so future upgrades are opt-in (Pass 1 B-1). Fallback: Letta per Q-J trigger. |\n| GBrain upstream stalls or pivots in S2-S5 timeframe (bus-factor â€” single author, 5-week-old project) | Medium | Medium | Vendored snapshot per above. Plan B mental experiment: list components we'd have to write ourselves if GBrain disappeared â€” queue as Pass-2-deferred work post-S1. Ecosystem has 3+ third-party tools building on GBrain (per Pass 2 research), so bus factor is distributed. |\n| Bun-as-required-runtime conflicts with existing Node/npm convention | Medium | Medium | Bun installs side-by-side with Node; isolated scope: use Bun *only* for GBrain operations, document in CLAUDE.md, integrate into Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1. |\n| **B-11 namespace rename touches 30+ brain-code files; test-gate could break** | Medium | High | Scripted find-and-replace `'gbrain'` â†’ `'gwl-corpus'`; full 498/498 test-suite re-run as the verify gate; rollback path is a `git revert` since rename lands in its own commit. ASR-loop bug in Setup-GWL-Server.ps1 may interact; verify before scheduling. |\n| t2r dispatcher latency (~2Ã— single-call) feels too slow for daily use | Low-Medium | High (kills John's adoption) | Top-tier-both is the v0 architectural commitment (Q2 walkthrough) â€” latency is a *measured* risk, not a tunable parameter; if too slow, S2 review captures it from real-use signal data and Â§11 contingency (b) provides the experiment branch. |\n| Cross-provider plumbing (Opus escalation crosses wallets) breaks `routing.json` or wallet enforcement | Low | Medium | Default config (Gemini Pro both) is single-provider; cross-provider only on Opus-escalation path which can be implemented after S1 ships. Schema extension lands S1 day-8; cross-provider exercising deferred to S2. |\n| $100/mo t2r wallet cap proves too tight even at Pro-both | Medium | Medium | Q1-Q2 precedence rule: raise the wallet, don't downgrade models. First wallet adjustment is *expected*, not failure (B-13). Revision triggers: first soft-alert hit, or end-of-S1 review, or John reports cap-friction. |\n| **GBrain's own LLM+embedding spend not in the $100 t2r wallet; could surprise on first month** (B-12) | Medium | Low-Medium | Separate $30/mo starting estimate for GBrain operational wallet; audit task in S2 right-sizes against real-use data; track on its own line in `logs/wallet-revisions.jsonl`. Confusion-avoidance: cap-hit on this line doesn't mean v0 t2r failure. |\n| v0 quality-signal capture overhead degrades agent responsiveness | Low | Medium | Async writes; fail-soft (signal write failure does not block the turn). |\n| Phase C Step A (Llama-3.1-8B install) blocks on HF account / Llama agreement / HF_TOKEN | Medium | Low (deferred to S3 anyway) | John handles HF account when convenient; S3 has slack. |\n| Memory `feedback_powershell_51_compat` is incomplete (gwl-server runs PS 5.1; some sprint scripts may want PS 7 for newer cmdlets) | Low | Low | `expert-coder-Win11` skill (shipped 2026-05-14) handles this. |\n| Coworkâ†”host bridge already live (2026-05-14) â€” does that change risk profile? | Low | Low-positive | Reduces script-emit risk; enables direct probes during sprints. Net: tooling improvement. |\n| Alpha persona file drifts from v0 reality | Mitigated | Low | S1 day-1/2 `PERSONA-DESIGN-Alpha-v0.md` memo + 5/26 rewrite; S2 audit confirms. |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Definition of done â€” v5 plan ratification\n\n**Status:** met\n\nThis plan is \"done\" per the SESSION-HANDOFF-V5 definition-of-done checklist. All items shipped:\n\n- [x] Current-state recap drawing on STATE-OF-PROJECT + Wave 7 close + Phase C scripts + today's tooling adds (Â§2)\n- [x] Explicit v4 â†’ v5 reframe acknowledged (brainâ‰ agent; agent-layer commoditized; GBrain adoption; quality-signal hooks) (Â§1)\n- [x] v0/v1/v2 spec table with brain layer + agent layer + sleep updates + wallet + success criterion (Â§3)\n- [x] v0 build plan â€” concrete, dated, decomposed into sprint sessions; days-to-weeks not months (Â§4)\n- [x] Parallel workstreams from v4 explicitly disposed (continue / defer / supersede) (Â§5)\n- [x] Refreshed gaps analysis as a sibling file ([GAPS-2026-05-14.md](./GAPS-2026-05-14.md)) â€” frozen at master-promotion\n- [x] Critique-ready section markers â€” every Â§ has a `Status:` line per project-manager skill discipline\n- [x] Two bounded critique passes complete (Pass 1 + Pass 2); no Pass 3\n- [x] Risk register populated (Â§8)\n- [x] Failure-mode contingencies named (Â§11)\n- [x] Cadence-sync mechanism defined (Â§12)\n\n---\n\n## 10. What's explicitly *not* in v5\n\n**Status:** locked from SESSION-HANDOFF \"parked\" list\n\nItems that v5 acknowledges as designed-and-deferred, not abandoned. Adding any of these to v5's critical path requires John's explicit approval.\n\n- Full plasticity catalog beyond first-plasticity (post-v2 future work)\n- FBB / PVB+P / Vulcan-Intuitionalist hemispheric work\n- Multiple brain architectures (each separately would warrant their own v5-analog plan)\n- Full K-12 curriculum run across two pilots (v4 Phase D)\n- Multi-cluster specialization (W / S / Math agents â€” the v4 cohort-spawning framing with manager agents) is **RE-OPENED** as of 2026-05-21 (Alpha-b0v1 phase). \n- **The Alpha-b0v1 Organization:** We will implement a hierarchical multi-agent system with:\n  1. **Ecgberht (Executive PA):** Global router and master interface.\n  2. **Per-Project PMs:** Dedicated agents (e.g., `pm-teaching`) with domain-isolated memory and skills.\n  3. **Specialist Clones:** Dynamic branching of code/finance/etc specialists bound to specific projects.\n  4. **Nightly Consolidation:** A \"Librarian\" loop to harvest and share learning globally.\n- **Wallet Guard:** This phase begins as a **Low-Volume Pilot**. Per-agent wallets are tiered ($30/$100/$5) and child clones inherit the parent's budget.\n- INFRA-2 (web admin portal)\n- INFRA-3 (mobile + voice)\n- Tournament 2 / 3 (Tournament 1 v2 is gated on Phase B operational data, which is unblocked but not prioritized)\n- Hemispheric ablation study\n- Letta â€” superseded by GBrain's retrieval; revisit only per Q-J sharpened trigger\n- Build-vs-buy on OpenClaw â€” John has chosen build/use; flagged for revisit if engineering cost compounds\n- **Forking GBrain (Plan B contingency, post-v0)** â€” if GBrain upstream stalls or develops unfixable bugs, vendor a known-good snapshot and maintain locally. Triggered by S2/S3 findings, not by default.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Failure-mode contingencies\n\n**Status:** locked from Pass 1 B-5 + Pass 2 amendment plan\n\nThe Q5 walkthrough decision (\"if v0 broadly doesn't work, we rethink the architecture\") needs concrete branches. Three contingencies are pre-named so the rethink starts from a position of context, not a blank page.\n\n**Triggered by:** S3 promote-gate evaluation against the per-workflow-type adoption matrix (Â§3, Â§4 S3).\n\n### Branch (a) â€” v0 works on most workflow types\n\nPer-workflow-type matrix shows â‰¥3 types green. **Proceed to v1 as drafted.** S4 scopes v1 cognitive-cell substrate.\n\n### Branch (b) â€” v0 works on some, fails on others\n\nMatrix shows 1-2 types green, others red. S4 = targeted patch via skill/tool/prompt iteration in the failing workflow types. **Do not promote to v1** until all critical types green. Specific patches per workflow type are spec'd from the signal data (which skill, which tool, which prompt segment of t2r).\n\n### Branch (c) â€” v0 broadly fails\n\nMatrix shows 0-1 types green across the board. S4 = \"rethink experiment.\" Three named candidate experiments to run (one per S4 sub-sprint or in parallel if resourceable):\n\n1. **Architecture experiment.** Swap t2r split for single-call (no taste/reasoning bifurcation) with thinner prompts on the same agent stack. Measure delta. Confirms whether t2r adds value vs raw single-frontier-call.\n2. **Model experiment.** Try Anthropic Opus on both halves (after raising the wallet per Q1-Q2 precedence). Measures quality lift from model substitution at top tier.\n3. **Runtime experiment.** Try Cowork's MCP integration with GBrain bolted in, *instead of* OpenClaw+GBrain. Lower switching cost than redesigning architecture; tests whether OpenClaw's runtime is contributing failure vs the t2r design.\n\nThe plan should never be a single thread. Each branch has a named first experiment ready to run.\n\n---","numLines":366,"startLine":1,"totalLines":510,"truncatedByTokenCap":true}}}
